 "captions": {
  "script": "This rainbow volcano wasn't made by nature. It was made by a mistake. Glitch Diary, entry nine. Fly Geyser, in the Nevada desert. In nineteen sixty-four, a geothermal company drilled a test well here. The water wasn't hot enough for power, so the well was left behind, never properly sealed. But that's not the strange part. Water hotter than ninety degrees Celsius kept pushing up, day and night. And the minerals it carried started building a mound of stone that is still growing, several inches every year. And there's one thing that makes it look truly unreal... Those reds and greens aren't paint. They're living microbes, heat-loving thermophiles that thrive in the scalding water. A human error, turned into a living sculpture. Would you visit it? Tell me in the comments. Follow for the next entry of my glitch diary. Because this mistake is still growing...",
